{
  "context": "Follow the pattern established by h2odb and amplab benchmarks (small, focused\nbenchmarks with synthetic data). Use benchbox/core/h2odb/ as a template for\ndirectory structure. Generate synthetic embedding vectors using numpy random\nwith controlled seeds for reproducibility. Use cosine similarity as the\ndefault distance function (most common in RAG applications).\n",
  "description": "Implement vector search benchmarking for OLAP databases with vector/embedding\nsupport. Test similarity search performance across platforms that support\nvector operations: BigQuery, Snowflake, Databricks, ClickHouse, PostgreSQL\n(pgvector), and DuckDB (vss extension).\n\nFocus on the core vector search operations used in RAG applications:\n- k-Nearest Neighbor (kNN) exact search\n- Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN) search with HNSW/IVF indexes\n- Filtered vector search (metadata + vector similarity)\n- Batch vector operations\n\nUse the ANN-Benchmarks methodology as a reference standard for measuring\nrecall@k vs queries-per-second tradeoffs.",
  "legacy": {
    "anti_patterns": [
      {
        "dont": "benchmark index build time in the power run",
        "instead": "measure it separately in the load phase",
        "item_id": "vector-search-benchmark-support",
        "why": "index creation is a one-time cost"
      },
      {
        "dont": "require vector database extensions to be pre-installed",
        "instead": "detect availability and skip gracefully with actionable error messages",
        "item_id": "vector-search-benchmark-support",
        "why": "platforms may not have them"
      },
      {
        "dont": "use real ML model embeddings for benchmark data",
        "instead": "use synthetic vectors with known statistical properties",
        "item_id": "vector-search-benchmark-support",
        "why": "model inference adds uncontrolled variability"
      }
    ],
